# Code owners for Scalar Commons.
#
# GitHub requests review from the owner of every path a PR touches. Combined
# with a branch protection rule on main requiring "Require review from Code
# Owners", this is what stops an agent-authored PR merging itself into the
# consensus, economic or CI layers unreviewed.
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS only *requests* review on its own. The blocking half is a
# branch protection setting on main, which cannot be configured from a file
# in the repository -- see docs/history/ROUND6.md "Remaining gaps".
#
# Order matters: later patterns win.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                   @0pStack

# ── T0/T1 paths: consensus, economics, the binary, and CI itself ───────────
# The runtime defines the economic rules and the supply cap.
/runtime/**         @0pStack
# Every pallet is a gaming surface (CLAUDE.md first principle 4).
/pallets/**         @0pStack
# The node is what actually produces blocks.
/node/**            @0pStack
# CI is the gate everything else is judged by, so it guards itself.
/.github/**         @0pStack

# ── Build, supply chain and operations ──────────────────────────────────────
# The dependency graph, toolchain and advisory ignores decide what gets built.
/Cargo.toml         @0pStack
/Cargo.lock         @0pStack
/rust-toolchain.toml @0pStack
/deny.toml          @0pStack
/.cargo/**          @0pStack
/package.json       @0pStack
/package-lock.json  @0pStack
# Root-key tools and live-host units run with real keys.
/scripts/**         @0pStack
/deploy/**          @0pStack
# Agent permissions, secret scanning and the rules agents follow.
/.claude/**         @0pStack
/factory/**         @0pStack
/.gitleaks.toml     @0pStack
/CLAUDE.md          @0pStack
/SECURITY.md        @0pStack
